<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I876008aac76895f542fe6cc330953181cbf92670" commit="91c74e52ae205978112e853a5b4b098430bbe921" commit_message="cryptohome: Avoid OpenSSL symbol collision  We plan to add OpenSSL 1.1 API support to all of platform2 via a unified compat layer provided by header &lt;crypto/libcrypto-compat.h&gt; installed by libchrome (crypto).  This header will #define LIBCRYPTO_COMPAT_H to identify itself.  It will also define compatibility rutines including the RSA_get0_key() defined here, making this blob obsolete.  However, we can't have the same symbol defined both here and by libchrome, so guard this local one so we can land the libchrome change.  BUG=chromium:737942 TEST=cros_workon --board=betty start chaps TEST=Apply patch to fix trunks for OpenSSL 1.1 TEST=w/ openssl-1.0.2r: FEATURES=test emerge-betty libchrome cryptohome TEST=w/ openssl-1.0.2r &amp; CL:555072: FEATURES=test emerge-betty libchrome cryptohome TEST=w/ openssl-1.1.0j &amp; CL:555072: FEATURES=test emerge-betty libchrome cryptohome   =&gt; In all cases, builds ok and passes unittests TEST=PreCQ  Change-Id: I876008aac76895f542fe6cc330953181cbf92670 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1658522 Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1658522" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/22/1658522/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id6be9c310261d9ae2e94cc75c5d6887c484b9ab4" commit="4cb697f192a60609177c0f79f48d2fad52d08678" commit_message="chaps: Use Scoped types in unittests  Use crypto::ScopedXXX types for RSA and BIGNUMs in unittests.  BUG=chromium:738288 TEST=FEATURES=test emerge-betty chaps  Change-Id: Id6be9c310261d9ae2e94cc75c5d6887c484b9ab4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1659951 Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1659951" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/51/1659951/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="Ia127ad21984759fb4d7fb3f1032f9888e91bab1f" commit="afaa71c45e06bac5976780bb47cf2d9011bc498e" commit_message="FIXUP: CHROMIUM: go2001: Modify alignment checks for buffers.  drivers/media/pci/go2001/go2001_driver.c: In function 'go2001_buf_init': drivers/media/pci/go2001/go2001_driver.c:288:4: warning:  format '%zu' expects argument of type 'size_t',  but argument 6 has type 'long unsigned int'  vb2_plane_size(), the parameter in question, indeed returns unsigned long.  BUG=chromium:430638 TEST=veatest on unaligned buffers  Change-Id: Ia127ad21984759fb4d7fb3f1032f9888e91bab1f Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1666697 Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Fletcher Woodruff &lt;fletcherw@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1666697" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/97/1666697/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="I13ec5558f5cb1edc804242b4b2136d1ce8b26122" commit="15e6a1bde754d475e92bbc971e47d466485ac626" commit_message="FIXUP: CHROMIUM: v4l: Add go2001 PCI codec driver.  The driver fails to build on many architectures, including arm and arm64, with the following error.  drivers/media/pci/go2001/go2001_hw.c: In function 'go2001_map_buffer': drivers/media/pci/go2001/go2001_hw.c:938:3: error:  implicit declaration of function 'dma_cache_sync'  dma_cache_sync() is indeed only defined for a few architectures in v4.14.y. Limit driver to X86 since that is the only architecture where the driver is actually usable and where it has been tested.  BUG=chromium:430638 TEST=video tests  Change-Id: I13ec5558f5cb1edc804242b4b2136d1ce8b26122 Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1666698 Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Fletcher Woodruff &lt;fletcherw@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1666698" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/98/1666698/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I65ee96e0dfabbeb4023c2dd60a97ad34ef328b86" commit="b8ea3ee41c555dff4c11b902a1b7d4b3742ca428" commit_message="libbrillo: Incorporate safe file handling code from arc-setup.  arc-setup had file handling functions that avoid TOCTOU issues. This moves those functions to libbrillo so they can be used throughout platform2 without depending on arc-setup.  BUG=chromium:896337 TEST=FEATURES=test emerge-${BOARD} libbrillo arc-setup  Change-Id: I65ee96e0dfabbeb4023c2dd60a97ad34ef328b86 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1646139 Tested-by: Allen Webb &lt;allenwebb@google.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Allen Webb &lt;allenwebb@google.com&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" 